Physical chemistry of interfaces and colloids — Diethelm Johannsmann (@cm-colloids-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_5FAT1MRFSVXVDS9Z6VCF4YM7TD
Diethelm Johannsmann, Institute of Physical Chemistry, TU Clausthal. *Physical Chemistry of Interfaces and Colloids*. [86-page institutional course notes, SS26 file](https://www.pc.tu-clausthal.de/fileadmin/Sites/PC/Documents/Vorlesungen/Colloids_Interfaces_SS26.pdf). Use this file identity rather than inventing an exact publication date from its directory or document metadata.

Read the whole course progressively. Sections 2–6 connect interfacial energy, capillarity, adsorption and wetting; section 7 develops surfactants; sections 10.5–10.10 develop ionic screening and colloid stability; section 11 connects dispersions to drying and films. Its cited original work extends the course treatment.

Contents and selected surfactant, screening, electrokinetic, colloid-stability and drying passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Page 68 was viewed visually to verify radicals and SI concentration conventions. Assigned reading is broader than this inspection. Simplified repulsion prefactors, generic drying rates and broad stability claims require their geometry and conditions before quantitative use. No blanket reuse licence was verified; numerous figures have separate credits. The notes remain an external reading.

} r_5FAT1MRFSVXVDS9Z6VCF4YM7TD
